------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software invoked at runtime (not redistributed by this project):
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* Ensembl VEP (Variant Effect Predictor)
    Apache License 2.0 — https://github.com/Ensembl/ensembl-vep

* OpenSpliceAI (default splice predictor)
    GPL-3.0 — https://github.com/Kuanhao-Chao/OpenSpliceAI
    Installed as a separate package and run as an independent program through
    its `openspliceai` command-line interface; no OpenSpliceAI code is included
    in or linked into HUVar. The OSAI-MANE models are downloaded by
    scripts/setup_data.py from the OpenSpliceAI distribution.

* SQUIRLS (optional; disabled by default)
    The Jackson Laboratory Software License Agreement for Non-Commercial Use —
    https://github.com/TheJacksonLaboratory/Squirls

* MMSplice (optional; disabled by default)
    MIT License — https://github.com/gagneurlab/MMSplice_MTSplice

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party data downloaded at runtime (not redistributed by this project):
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* ClinVar (NCBI)
    Public domain — https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/clinvar/intro/

* CIViC — Clinical Interpretation of Variants in Cancer (https://civicdb.org)
    CC0 1.0 — downloaded by scripts/setup_data.py --only civic (somatic OS2/SBS2).
    Cite: Griffith M et al., Nat Genet 2017;49:170-174; Krysiak K et al., Nucleic
    Acids Res 2023;51:D1230-D1241.

* gnomAD (Genome Aggregation Database)
    Released without restriction on use — https://gnomad.broadinstitute.org/terms

* ClinGen Dosage Sensitivity and Gene-Disease Validity curations
    CC0 1.0 — https://clinicalgenome.org/docs/terms-of-use/
    ClinGen requests attribution and the date accessed.

* NIH Clinical Genomic Database (CGD)
    https://research.nih.gov/cgd/

* Ensembl reference genome / transcript annotation
    https://www.ensembl.org/info/about/legal/index.html

* UCSC phyloP100way and RepeatMasker tracks
    https://genome.ucsc.edu/conditions.html (credit the data contributors)

* ESM1b precomputed variant-effect scores (default missense predictor)
    Brandes N et al., Nat Genet 2023;55:1512-1522.
    MIT License — https://github.com/ntranoslab/esm-variants

* AlphaMissense (optional)
    Predictions: CC BY 4.0; code: Apache License 2.0 —
    https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphamissense

* REVEL (optional)
    Free for non-commercial use; commercial use requires a separate licence —
    https://sites.google.com/site/revelgenomics/

* FuncVEP-CTI precomputed scores (optional)
    Kayaalp E et al., Nat Genet 2026. Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.18432730.
    PolyForm Strict License 1.0.0 — NON-COMMERCIAL use only, and the data may
    not be redistributed. HUVar neither bundles nor downloads it by default:
    stage it locally with `setup_data.py --with-funcvep` and select it with
    `--insilico-tool funcvep`.

* CADD (optional)
    Free for non-commercial use; commercial use requires a licence from the
    University of Washington (UW CoMotion) — https://cadd.bihealth.org/

* BayesDel (optional)
    https://fenglab.chpc.utah.edu/BayesDel/BayesDel.html
    No licence is stated by the provider; treated as non-commercial by HUVar.

* SpliceAI precomputed scores (optional)
    Free for academic/non-commercial research. Commercial use requires a
    separate license from Illumina.

REVEL, FuncVEP, CADD, BayesDel and SpliceAI are never read in the default configuration
(ESM1b + OpenSpliceAI); users who enable them must obtain the data themselves
and comply with the upstream terms.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party data redistributed in resources/ (derived tables):
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* ClinGen Criteria Specification Registry (CSpec) and Evidence Repository (eRepo)
    resources/clingen/cspec_json/, resources/clingen/CSpecList.tsv,
    resources/<assembly>/erepo_*.tsv and the tables in resources/shared/ that
    are mined from the VCEP specifications (disease_prevalence*.tsv,
    pm1_hotspots.tsv, pm4_regions.tsv, vcep_comparator_rules.tsv,
    vcep_pvs1_*exons.tsv, ps1_paralog_map.tsv [SCN VCEP paralogue table],
    tp53_pp3_bp4_codes.tsv [ClinGen TP53 VCEP PP3/BP4 code table]).
    CC0 1.0 — https://clinicalgenome.org/docs/terms-of-use/
    Snapshot dates are listed in resources/shared/bundled_data_versions.tsv.

* NCBI RefSeq / MANE annotation
    resources/gff/ and resources/shared/mane_*.tsv are derived from the NCBI
    GRCh37 RefSeq GFF and MANE Release v1.5 (https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/refseq/MANE/).
    NCBI data are in the public domain (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/home/about/policies/).

* Cancer Hotspots, Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center
  (https://www.cancerhotspots.org/#/home)
    ODC Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0 — https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
    resources/clingen/cancerhotspots_TP53.tsv and cancerhotspots_VHL.tsv are
    unmodified exports (retrieved 2026-10-17). The TP53 and VHL rows of
    resources/shared/pm1_hotspots.tsv are derived from them as specified by the
    respective VCEPs and are likewise made available under the ODbL.
    See resources/clingen/LICENSE-CancerHotspots.md.
    Cite: Chang MT et al., Cancer Discov 2018;8:174-183; Chang MT et al.,
    Nat Biotechnol 2016;34:155-163.

* NCI TP53 Database, release R21 (Jan 2025) — https://tp53.cancer.gov
    resources/shared/tp53_functional.tsv is derived from MutationView_r21.csv,
    FunctionIshiokaDownload_r21.csv and FunctionDownload_r21.csv (assay classes
    from Kato et al. 2003, Giacomelli et al. 2018, Kotler et al. 2018 and
    Kawaguchi et al. 2005). The database terms allow the data to be freely
    accessed, used, downloaded and reproduced with appropriate acknowledgement,
    and prohibit any use that results in direct or indirect monetization
    (https://tp53.cancer.gov/about). The table is used only when
    --with-tp53-functional is given (off by default).
    Cite: The TP53 Database (R21, Jan 2025): https://tp53.cancer.gov;
    de Andrade KC et al., Cell Death Differ 2022;29:1071-1073.

* MaveDB (https://www.mavedb.org) bulk dump 2026-06-24 (Zenodo record 20840937)
    CC0 1.0 Universal — the dump contains only published, CC0-licensed data.
    resources/shared/mavedb_functional.tsv.gz and mavedb_scoresets.tsv are derived
    from it (score sets with clinical score calibrations; scripts/build_mavedb_functional.py).
    Cite: Rubin AF et al., Genome Biol 2025 (MaveDB 2024); the publication of each
    score set (listed in mavedb_scoresets.tsv); calibrations by the IGVF Coding
    Variant Focus Group and the score-set investigators.

* ClinGen ENIGMA BRCA1 and BRCA2 VCEP Specifications, Table 9 V1.2 (2024-11-18)
    resources/shared/enigma_brca12_table9.tsv is a tab-separated transcription of the
    table (scripts/build_enigma_table9.py). https://cspec.genome.network/cspec/ui/svi/doc/GN092
    Cite: Parsons MT et al., Am J Hum Genet 2024;111:2044-2058.

* Network of Cancer Genes (NCG 7.1), http://network-cancer-genes.org/
    Freely available; no licence required. resources/shared/somatic_gene_roles.tsv
    is derived from NCG_cancerdrivers_annotation_supporting_evidence.tsv (canonical
    drivers and their majority-vote role; scripts/build_somatic_resources.py) with
    curated corrections in somatic_gene_role_overrides.tsv.
    Cite: Dressler L et al., Genome Biol 2022;23:35.

* cancerhotspots.org v2 (Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center)
    Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/
    resources/shared/cancer_hotspots_v2.tsv is a derived database (residue and
    in-frame indel hotspots with sample counts, from hotspots_v2.xls of
    https://github.com/cBioPortal/cancerhotspots) and is made available under the
    same ODbL 1.0 licence; it is not covered by the Apache License of this project.
    Cite: Chang MT et al., Cancer Discov 2018;8:174-183; Chang MT et al.,
    Nat Biotechnol 2016;34:155-163.

* OncoTree (Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center), release 2025-10-03
    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 — https://github.com/cBioPortal/oncotree
    resources/shared/oncotree_doid.tsv is derived from it (codes, names, parents; mapped
    to Disease Ontology by scripts/build_tumor_ontology.py).
    Cite: Kundra R et al., JCO Clin Cancer Inform 2021;5:221-230.

* Human Disease Ontology, release 2026-09-30
    CC0 1.0 — https://github.com/DiseaseOntology/HumanDiseaseOntology
    resources/shared/doid_hierarchy.tsv (terms and is_a parents) is derived from doid.obo.
    Cite: Baron JA et al., Nucleic Acids Res 2024;52:D1305-D1314.

